# Mohawk marketing assets (site & app-adjacent art)

## Product tone

- **Mohawk** is an **indie, slightly rebellious RSS reader** — raw wire, user agency, not corporate news.
- Visuals should feel **chosen**, not sold: editorial street/documentary, not stock “diverse team laughing at laptop.”

## Audience (who should recognize themselves)

- **Age:** early 30s through early 50s.
- **Lives:** professionals, bartenders, tradespeople, creatives — **different jobs, same taste**.
- **Values:** culture, options, depth, independence; they read, listen, argue, and curate.

## What they have in common (show this, not demographics)

- **Curiosity** — scanning a shelf, a feed, a street poster, a menu of possibilities.
- **Taste** — worn-in quality (good coat, good boots, good bar, good bookshop), not club flash or luxury gloss.
- **Agency** — one person choosing while another is elsewhere doing their own thing (split frame OK); never “targeted at you” smile.

## Face policy (strict)

- **Do not show recognizable faces** of human subjects unless the user **explicitly** asks for faces in that request.
- Default framing: **from behind**, **over-shoulder** (face out of frame), **cropped above shoulders**, **in shadow/hat/hood**, **reflections without readable face**, **hands + object** (phone, paper, book spine).
- Crowds: anonymous backs and silhouettes only.

## What to avoid

- Nightlife / hookup / “gritty for grit’s sake” as the default mood.
- Generic hot-nightclub casting (miniskirts + heels as the hero grammar).
- Readable UI mockups or logos unless requested.
- Fantasy illustration; stay **photoreal** and **grounded** (near-future city OK per tower rules).

## Cast continuity (when models appear)

- Reference models 1 & 2 remain useful as **silhouette + wardrobe** cues from behind; update wardrobe toward **taste-forward indie** when scenes call for it (see `mohawk-scene-characters.mdc`).
- Mohawk figure (black mohawk, patched jacket): same face policy unless hero shot specifies otherwise.

